Now I have a much better understanding of the codebase. Let me check how the events are fetched and grouped. The issue is with the `loadEvents` function and how it handles pagination when filtering by source.

Let me look more carefully at the loadEvents function and handleLoadMore:

```javascript
const loadEvents = useCallback(async (pageNum = 0, isLoadMore = false) => {
    if (isLoadMore) {
      setLoadingMore(true);
    } else {
      setLoading(true);
    }

    try {
      // Fetch events from Supabase (production only)
      const result = await fetchEvents();
      const data = result.events || [];
      const sources = result.sources || [];

      if (isLoadMore) {
        setEvents(prev => [...prev, ...data]);  // <-- PROBLEM: Appends without deduplication
      } else {
        setEvents(data);
        setAvailableSources(sources);
      }
      setPage(pageNum);
    } catch (err) {
      setError(err.message);
      console.error('Failed to load events:', err);
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
      setLoadingMore(false);
    }
  }, []);
```

The `handleLoadMore`:
```javascript
const handleLoadMore = useCallback(() => {
    // Only allow loading more when no filters are active
    // This prevents API calls when user scrolls to end of filtered list
    if (!loadingMore && !loading && !timeFilter && selectedCategories.length === 0) {
      loadEvents(page + 1, true);
    }
  }, [loadingMore, loading, loadEvents, page, timeFilter, selectedCategories]);
```

The problem I see:
1. `handleLoadMore` is triggered when the user scrolls to the end
2. It only checks if `!timeFilter && selectedCategories.length === 0`, but it DOESN'T check if `selectedProvider` is set


3. When a provider is selected, `loadEvents` still appends new data without deduplication, and the function fetches all events again rather than paginating by provider. Since Supabase returns the same full dataset on every call, appending it creates duplicates and breaks pagination logic.

Looking at the data flow: `fetchEvents()` in eventServiceClient.js retrieves 100 events without any source filtering. When `loadEvents` runs again with `isLoadMore=true`, it appends the identical dataset to the existing events, causing duplication. The root issue is that pagination doesn't actually paginate—it just refetches the same data repeatedly without offset or provider-specific filtering.

The Stockholm source being selected in the UI triggers this bug because filtering happens client-side after data loads, but the underlying pagination mechanism never accounts for the selected provider filter. Each scroll triggers another full fetch, which gets appended rather than being distinct pages of filtered results. The API always returns the same 100 events regardless of pagination attempts. When `handleLoadMore` triggers, it appends the identical dataset to what's already rendered, causing duplication on the frontend. I need to add deduplication logic to prevent the same events from appearing multiple times.
